+# Codex registration panel browser check
+
+This optional fixture renders the actual React component and Silo CSS in Chromium.
+Only Tauri's `invoke` transport is mocked. It does not exercise native dialogs,
+Codex registration, SSH, or macOS application integration.
+
+From `app/SiloUI`, run a loopback-only Vite server:
+
+```sh
+npm run dev -- --host 127.0.0.1 --port 1425
+```
+
+Use an existing Python environment containing Playwright and an existing Chromium
+binary (no production dependency or startup download is added):
+
+```sh
+python tests/registration-panel/check.py \
+  --chromium /absolute/path/to/chromium \
+  --output /absolute/path/to/test-artifacts
+```
+
+The check uses owned synthetic data, validates 360px/1280px layout bounds, full
+keyboard navigation, focus after feedback/cancellation, native-picker cancellation,
+explicit review confirmation, and stale feedback after path edits. It writes
+screenshots and `after.json` into the specified artifact directory. The browser
+runs headlessly with `--no-sandbox` for the isolated test VM; this is not a product
+launch configuration. Stop the Vite process when finished.
